Penegakan hukum pidana siber mengintegrasikan hukum acara pidana umum (KUHAP) dengan prosedur khusus dalam Pasal 43 UU ITE:

1. Kewenangan Penyidik Siber:
Penyidikan kejahatan siber dilakukan oleh Penyidik Kepolisian RI (khususnya Direktorat Tindak Pidana Siber / Dittipidsiber Bareskrim Polri) dan Penyidik Pegawai Negeri Sipil (PPNS) Kementerian Kominfo. Wewenang khusus penyidik meliputi:
- Melakukan penggeledahan dan penyitaan sistem komputer, server, telepon seluler, dan media penyimpanan elektronik;
- Meminta keterangan ahli di bidang teknologi informasi dan forensik digital;
- Memerintahkan PSE memutus akses sementara terhadap sistem atau data yang menjadi objek kejahatan;
- Meminta data rekaman lalu lintas komunikasi (traffic data) dan log server dari Internet Service Provider (ISP) atau penyedia telekomunikasi atas izin pengadilan.

2. Standar Pengelolaan Bukti Digital dan Rantai Penjagaan (Chain of Custody):
Bukti digital memiliki sifat volatil, mudah bermutasi, dan rentan terhadap kontaminasi data. Berdasarkan Peraturan Kapolri No. 10 Tahun 2009 dan standar forensik internasional ISO/IEC 27037, penyitaan bukti digital harus memenuhi tahapan ketat:
- Identifikasi & Pengamanan: Memutus koneksi jaringan fisik/nirkabel (menggunakan Faraday bag) untuk mencegah penghapusan data jarak jauh (remote wiping);
- Akuisisi Forensik: Melakukan kloning atau pencitraan bit-stream (bit-stream image) terhadap hard drive atau memori, tanpa pernah mengubah media penyimpanan asli;
- Verifikasi Nilai Hash: Menghitung nilai hash matematis (algoritma SHA-256 atau MD5) pada bukti asli dan bukti salinan forensik. Nilai hash wajib identik 100%;
- Dokumentasi Berita Acara Rantai Penjagaan (Chain of Custody Form): Mencatat secara kronologis siapa yang mengambil, memindahkan, menguji, dan menyimpan bukti. Cacat pada rantai penjagaan dapat menyebabkan bukti digital dinyatakan tidak sah di persidangan.

3. Peran Keterangan Ahli Forensik Digital di Pengadilan:
Keterangan ahli forensik digital yang disumpah berfungsi merekonstruksi lini masa kejahatan (timeline analysis), membuktikan kepemilikan akun/penulis pesan (authorship identification), merecover berkas yang dihapus (file carving), serta mengkorelasikan log telemetri IP address dengan lokasi fisik tersangka, memberikan kekuatan pembuktian ilmiah (scientific crime investigation) yang mengikat pertimbangan hakim.

sections.content_en:
The enforcement of cybercrime offenses harmonizes general criminal procedural law (KUHAP) with specialized procedural powers codified under Article 43 of the ITE Law:

1. Investigatory Jurisdiction and Powers:
Cyber investigations are conducted by Indonesian National Police investigators (specifically the Directorate of Cyber Crimes / Dittipidsiber Bareskrim Polri) and Civil Servant Investigators (PPNS) of the Ministry of Communication and Informatics. Specialized investigative competencies include:
- Executing search and seizure warrants over servers, endpoints, smartphones, and volatile digital storage arrays;
- Summonsing accredited information technology and digital forensics expert witnesses;
- Ordering PSEs to enact temporary access freezes over systems or data involved in criminal conduct;
- Demanding subscriber telecommunications traffic data and ISP audit connection logs with judicial authorization.

2. Digital Evidence Management and Chain of Custody (ISO/IEC 27037):
Digital evidence is inherently volatile, easily mutable, and susceptible to latent data corruption. Pursuant to National Police Regulation No. 10 of 2009 and global forensic standards (ISO/IEC 27037), evidentiary preservation requires rigorous protocols:
- Identification & Containment: Severing physical and wireless network connectivity (deploying signal-shielding Faraday isolation bags) to prevent remote wiping or unauthorized cloud sync;
- Forensic Acquisition: Generating bit-stream forensic images of volatile memory and non-volatile storage, preserving original media without alteration;
- Cryptographic Hash Calculation: Computing cryptographic hashes (SHA-256 or MD5 algorithms) across original and cloned drives. Matching hash values verify exact bit-level integrity;
- Chain of Custody Ledger Documentation: Chronologically recording every transfer, custody transfer, testing methodology, and repository location. Any unexplained gap in the chain of custody fatally undermines evidentiary admissibility before trial judges.

3. Probative Authority of Digital Forensics Expert Testimony:
Sworn digital forensic expert reports reconstruct empirical event timelines, substantiate digital authorship, execute deleted data carving, and correlate server IP telemetry with cellular tower positioning, providing rigorous scientific crime investigation standards that anchor judicial convictions.

