Arsitektur keamanan dan ketahanan ruang siber nasional dikoordinasikan secara terpusat oleh Badan Siber dan Sandi Negara (BSSN):

1. Kedudukan dan Wewenang BSSN (Perpres No. 28 Tahun 2021):
BSSN bertindak sebagai lembaga pemerintah yang bertanggung jawab langsung kepada Presiden dalam merumuskan dan melaksanakan kebijakan keamanan siber, persandian, penanggulangan insiden siber, serta diplomasi siber internasional. BSSN mengoperasikan Pusat Operasi Keamanan Siber Nasional (Pusopskamsinas) dan mengoordinasikan tim tanggap insiden siber (Computer Security Incident Response Team / CSIRT) di seluruh kementerian, lembaga, dan pemerintah daerah.

2. Pelindungan Infrastruktur Informasi Vital (IIV - Perpres No. 82 Tahun 2022):
Infrastruktur Informasi Vital adalah sistem elektronik yang memanfaatkan teknologi informasi dan/atau operasional yang jika mengalami gangguan, kerusakan, atau kehancuran dapat berdampak serius terhadap kedaulatan negara, keamanan nasional, perekonomian, pelayanan publik, atau keselamatan masyarakat. Cakupan IIV meliputi 8 sektor strategis:
- Administrasi Pemerintahan;
- Energi dan Sumber Daya Mineral;
- Transportasi;
- Keuangan dan Perbankan;
- Kesehatan;
- Teknologi Informasi dan Komunikasi;
- Pertanian dan Pangan; serta
- Pertahanan dan Keamanan Negara.
Pengelola IIV wajib menerapkan manajemen risiko siber, standar keamanan informasi berbasis SNI ISO/IEC 27001, audit berkala, arsitektur pertahanan berlapis (defense-in-depth), serta melaporkan insiden siber berkategori darurat kepada BSSN paling lambat 1 x 24 jam.

3. Standardisasi Kriptografi Nasional:
BSSN memegang otoritas pengujian dan sertifikasi terhadap algoritma dan perangkat persandian yang digunakan dalam transmisi informasi rahasia pertahanan, diplomasi luar negeri, dan komunikasi kepresidenan guna mencegah spionase dan penyadapan oleh aktor ancaman persisten tingkat lanjut (Advanced Persistent Threats / APT).

sections.content_en:
Indonesia's sovereign cybersecurity architecture and digital defense apparatus are strategically unified under the National Cyber and Crypto Agency (Badan Siber dan Sandi Negara - BSSN):

1. Statutory Mandate of BSSN (Presidential Regulation No. 28 of 2021):
BSSN serves as the supreme national agency reporting directly to the President, charged with formulating and executing cybersecurity doctrine, state cryptographic architecture, emergency cyber incident response, and cyber diplomacy. BSSN runs the National Cyber Security Operations Center (Pusopskamsinas) and orchestrates institutional Computer Security Incident Response Teams (CSIRTs) across all ministries, state organs, and regional governments.

2. Protection of Critical Information Infrastructure (IIV - Presidential Regulation No. 82 of 2022):
Critical Information Infrastructure (IIV) comprises electronic systems utilizing information and/or operational technologies whose disruption, damage, or destruction would generate severe consequences for state sovereignty, national security, economic stability, public health, or human safety. IIV encompasses eight strategic sectors:
- Public Administration;
- Energy and Mineral Resources;
- Transportation;
- Banking and Financial Services;
- Healthcare;
- Information and Communication Technology;
- Agriculture and Food Supply; and
- Defense and National Security.
Operators of designated critical assets are mandated to enforce ISO/IEC 27001-aligned cyber risk management frameworks, conduct recurring technical security audits, deploy defense-in-depth security architectures, and immediately notify BSSN of critical cyber compromises within 24 hours.

3. Sovereign Cryptographic Standards:
BSSN retains exclusive authority over the verification, testing, and operational certification of cryptographic ciphers and encryption hardware securing classified diplomatic communications, cabinet-level interactions, and sovereign military systems against foreign state-sponsored Advanced Persistent Threats (APTs).
